research/audit/wave3-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:31:{"id":"def-rational-power","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/realanal.pdf","https://mathcenter.oxford.emory.edu/site/math100/radicals/"],"rationale":"Lebl’s Basic Analysis exercises give Bernoulli, unique positive nth roots, rational-power well-definedness and monotonicity, while the Emory notes give the principal-root and negative-base restrictions semantically matching “Rational powers $a^r$ of a positive base”. The item adapts the established result to a complete ordered field, the library’s positive-base convention, and its explicit zero and rational-exponent boundary clauses. It has no proof component. The local wording and, where present, proof decomposition are not exact-source matches, so each supplied component is conservatively classified as shown; no component is labeled ai-generated merely because an exact transcription did not surface. URL verification route: model-side web open returned content for every recorded URL on 2026-08-04 (HTTP 200); shell DNS was not used.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
