research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r6-thm-mean-value-inequality.prompt.md:3043:2.3 **Clauses 3 and 4.** The same substitution in [L6] turns the Lipschitz condition into $|f(x) - f(x')| \le L\,|x-x'|$ for all $x,x' \in A$, and the $\alpha$-Hölder condition into $|f(x) - f(x')| \le C\,|x-x'|^{\alpha}$, the power being that of [[def-rational-power]] and defined at $x = x'$ by the convention $0^{\alpha} = 0$ recorded in [L6]. Since this library gives no other definition of the two conditions for a real function on $A$, the displayed inequalities are what those words mean here. [step 1.1, L6]
